"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Boner","party":"R","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Ide","party":"R","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Pearson","party":"R","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Steinmetz","party":"R","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":10,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-03-08","text":"Assigned Chapter Number 87","chamber":"Governor"},{"date":"2026-03-08","text":"Governor Signed HEA No. 0027","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-03-06","text":"S President Signed HEA No. 0027","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-03-06","text":"H Speaker Signed HEA No. 0027","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-03-05","text":"Assigned Number HEA No. 0027","chamber":"Governor"},{"date":"2026-03-05","text":"S 3rd Reading:Passed 29-2-0-0-0","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-03-04","text":"S 2nd Reading:Passed","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-03-03","text":"S COW:Passed","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"S Placed on General File","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-27","text":"S01 - Judiciary:Recommend Do Pass 3-0-2-0-0","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-24","text":"S Introduced and Referred to S01 - Judiciary","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-23","text":"S Received for Introduction","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-02-22","text":"H 3rd Reading:Passed 58-3-1-0-0","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-20","text":"H 2nd Reading:Passed","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-20","text":"H COW:Passed","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-16","text":"H Placed on General File","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-16","text":"H02 - Appropriations:Recommend Do Pass 6-1-0-0-0","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-10","text":"H Introduced and Referred to H02 - Appropriations 57-4-1-0-0","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-05","text":"H Received for Introduction","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-02-04","text":"Bill Number Assigned","chamber":"Governor"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2026/HB0096","textUrl":"https://wyoleg.gov/2026/Enroll/HB0096.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Enrolled","date":null,"url":"https://wyoleg.gov/2026/Enroll/HB0096.pdf","type":"PDF"},{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://wyoleg.gov/2026/Introduced/HB0096.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[{"date":"2026-03-05","motion":"S 3rd Reading:Passed 29-2-0-0-0","result":"pass","chamber":"Senate","counts":{"yes":29,"no":2}},{"date":"2026-02-27","motion":"S01 - Judiciary:Recommend Do Pass 3-0-2-0-0","result":"pass","chamber":"Senate","counts":{"yes":3,"no":0,"excused":2}},{"date":"2026-02-22","motion":"H 3rd Reading:Passed 58-3-1-0-0","result":"pass","chamber":"House","counts":{"yes":58,"no":3,"excused":1}},{"date":"2026-02-16","motion":"H02 - Appropriations:Recommend Do Pass 6-1-0-0-0","result":"pass","chamber":"House","counts":{"yes":6,"no":1}},{"date":"2026-02-10","motion":"H Introduced and Referred to H02 - Appropriations 57-4-1-0-0","result":"pass","chamber":"House","counts":{"yes":57,"no":4,"excused":1}}],"documents":[{"label":"Bill Digest","date":null,"url":"https://wyoleg.gov/2026/Digest/HB0096.pdf","type":"PDF"},{"label":"Fiscal Note","date":null,"url":"https://wyoleg.gov/2026/Fiscal/HB0096.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The measure lowers the minimum age for a concealed-carry permit from 21 to 18 in Wyoming. It also removes old rules tied to permits for people ages 18 to 21.","aiSummaryBasis":"official summary","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"WY-2026-HB69":{"id":"WY-2026-HB69","passed":true,"number":"HB 69","title":"Department of health-land transfers.","summary":"This act authorizes and directs the Department of Health to convey a specified parcel of land in Fremont County to the Wyoming Department of Transportation. The land parcel is currently held for the Wyoming State Training School, and this conveyance must be made without impact other rights and estates and without the payment of consideration, except the Department of Transportation must pay closing and title-insurance costs. This act also authorizes and directs the Department of Health to convey a different parcel of land held for the Wyoming State Training School. This conveyance is subject to all of the following:The conveyance must comply with statutes governing the sale of state lands.The conveyance must be made without impacting other rights or estates.The parcel, or portions of the parcel, may be disposed of in one (1) or more conveyances.The purchaser must pay all costs associated with surveys, title insurance, and closing.The purchaser of the parcel or any portion of the parcel must agree that the sole use of the parcel shall be for residential housing. For both transactions, the Department of Health must consult with the city of Lander, the Board of Land Commissioners, and the Office of State Lands and Investments. This act requires the Department of Transportation to report to the Joint Transportation, Highways, and Military Affairs Interim Committee after the land transfers are finalized. Comments: This act requires the Department of Transportation to report to the Joint Transportation, Highways, and Military Affairs Interim Committee.This act is effective immediately.","summarySource":"Wyoming legislature, summary (via Open States)","introduced":"2026-01-29","sponsor":{"name":"Larsen, L","party":"R","state":"WY","district":"54"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Posey","party":"D","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Case","party":"R","state":"WY","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":2,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-03-08","text":"Assigned Chapter Number 97","chamber":"Governor"},{"date":"2026-03-08","text":"Governor Signed HEA No. 0039","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-03-06","text":"S President Signed HEA No. 0039","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-03-06","text":"H Speaker Signed HEA No. 0039","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-